# Ferite Tool - System Automation and Prototyping Script

## Overview
Ferite is a lightweight, interpreted scripting language designed for rapid prototyping and system automation tasks. This tool provides an environment to write, execute, and debug Ferite scripts.

## Features
- Lightweight interpreter for Ferite scripts.
- Support for system commands and process management.
- Basic data structures and control flow.
- File I/O operations.

## Usage
To execute a Ferite script, use the following command:

```bash
ferite_tool/main.ferite script.ferite
```

## Example

```ferite
print("Hello, World!");
var x = 10;
if (x > 5) {
    print("x is greater than 5");
}
```

